[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds
three problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October; that settled two of them, not the third.

<Callout kind="warn">
Still open: <code>shift</code>, dates moving one day ([#3]({issues.shift})). Neither the parser fix nor
retiring booking-v3 touches it. Reports like it still belong on #3, not on #4471.
</Callout>

## Where each one stands

- **`parser`**: fixed by engineering, `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. [#1]({issues.parser}) closed.
- **`hint`**: won't fix; the booking-v3 form is retired. [#2]({issues.hint}) closed as not planned.
- **`shift`**: open. No fix yet. [#3]({issues.shift}).

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} {labels} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day first, so
any day of 12 or less comes out swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. This is what #4471 says it is, and it is
most of the reports. Ticket: [#1]({issues.parser}).

**`hint`: booking-v3's form hints `MM/DD/YYYY` and reads the date day first.** People type what the hint
tells them, and the form reads it the tenant's way. It looks like the parser bug, but it only comes in
through the form, only from tenants on booking-v3, and the parser fix won't touch it. The desk's own
cause table already marks it "not this ticket — no ticket of its own". Ticket: [#2]({issues.hint}).

**`shift`: dates move one day, not a swap.** Tuesday shows as Monday; the same meeting lands on different
days in Lisbon and Toronto; an invite arrives before the booking was made. That is a date going through
a time zone and losing a day. The desk read these as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`) but left them
filed under the parser. Ticket: [#3]({issues.shift}).

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line, and the desk merged further
by hand: #4471 holds a dozen different subjects. The subject says *the date is wrong*; it can't say *why*.
Intake's tag doesn't help either: it is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the
problem on many reports (see the note under the table).

## For the desk

- Before marking a big ticket known, run its reports through `causeOf`
  ([triage](/kb/triage/dedupe)) and the one-day notes. More than one problem: split it.
- #4471 is closed, so new one-day reports go to [#3]({issues.shift}). A date swapped on a day-first
  tenant after 5 October is a new problem: the parser fix should have stopped those.
- Counts on this page are the desk's own view: built from `reports-4471.json` at render time with
  `causes.ts`, the same way as the cause table on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471).

